WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.483
The operating system and runtime stack determine how easy the lab is to operate after the first successful demo.

00:00:07.483 --> 00:00:13.495
Windows can be convenient for desktop workflows, vendor tools, and mixed productivity use.

00:00:13.495 --> 00:00:19.308
Linux is common for server-style operation, containers, driver control, and automation.

00:00:19.308 --> 00:00:26.256
Some users choose dual boot or a dedicated lab system to keep experiments away from a daily workstation.

00:00:26.256 --> 00:00:29.797
The best choice is the one you can maintain reliably.

00:00:29.797 --> 00:00:33.137
GPU drivers are a foundation, not an afterthought.

00:00:33.137 --> 00:00:39.684
Many AI runtimes depend on specific driver behavior, acceleration libraries, or container support.

00:00:39.684 --> 00:00:44.494
Once a stable configuration works, document it before changing versions.

00:00:44.494 --> 00:00:49.238
Driver updates can improve support, but they can also break a workflow.

00:00:49.238 --> 00:00:59.192
A lab should have an update discipline: know what is installed, why it is installed, and how you would return to a working state if an upgrade fails.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:09.080
The runtime stack may include container runtimes, Python environments, local inference runtimes, model managers, web frontends, notebooks, and APIs.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:12.754
These components change quickly, so separation matters.

00:01:12.754 --> 00:01:20.437
Keep the base system stable while experiments change in containers, virtual environments, or dedicated directories.

00:01:20.437 --> 00:01:27.519
Avoid letting every tool install global dependencies until the machine becomes impossible to reason about.

00:01:27.519 --> 00:01:30.793
Documentation is a practical reliability control.

00:01:30.793 --> 00:01:39.211
Record installation commands, driver versions, model locations, service ports, environment variables, and configuration files.

00:01:39.211 --> 00:01:43.019
This does not need to be formal enterprise documentation.

00:01:43.019 --> 00:01:50.902
A simple lab notebook can save hours when you rebuild, troubleshoot, compare performance, or explain your setup later.

00:01:50.902 --> 00:01:57.516
A homelab becomes more valuable when the environment can be recreated instead of merely remembered.
